{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>You have done</b> — twice in the Masorah: this one and the other: עשיתן תועבה in Ezekiel. As stated in the first chapter of Sotah, Pharaoh demanded that the midwives be subservient to him, for we find likewise regarding arayot, as it is written: כי את כל התועבות האל" "<b>And they kept alive</b> — twice in this parashah. As stated in the first chapter of Sotah: it was not enough that they did not kill them, but they even supplied them with water and food."], :book :exodus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {0 "The phrase עשיתן תועבה appears in Ezekiel 16:43. The citation of Sotah refers to Sotah 11b. The final quoted phrase 'כי את כל התועבות האל' appears in Ezekiel 16:51.", 1 "The citation refers to Sotah 11b."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:11:40.584469135Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}